speechtext:
That this House concur in Interim Supply as follows:
That this House do concur in Interim Supply as follows:
That a sum not exceeding $13,880,999,941.94 being composed of:
(1)	three-twelfths ($9,564,918,577.25) of the total of the amounts of the items set forth in the Main Estimates for the fiscal year ending March 31, 1994, which were laid upon the Table Thursday, February 25, 1993, and except for those items below:
(2)	eleven-twelfths of the total of the amounts ofTransport Votes 15 and 45 (Schedule A) of the said Estimates, $5,185,583.33;
(3)	nine-twelfths of the total of the amount of Treasury Board Vote 5 (Schedule B) of the said Estimates, $337,500,000.00;
(4)	seven-twelfths of the total of the amount of Labour Vote 15 (Schedule C) of the said Estimates, $1,072,750.00;
(5)	six-twelfths of the total of the amounts of Employment and Immigration Vote 5, and External Affairs Vote 15, and Indian Affairs and Northern Development Votes 10 and 45, and Industry, Science and Technology Vote 30, and Solicitor General Vote 5 (Schedule D) of the said Estimates, $650,959,100.00;
(6)	five-twelfths of the total of the amounts of Fisheries and Oceans Vote 10, and Indian Affairs and Northern Development Votes 5,15 and L25, and Public Works Vote 20, and Solicitor General Vote 40, and Transport Vote 1 (Schedule E) of the said Estimates, $1,669,800,500.01;
(7)	four-twelfths of the total of the amounts of Communications Votes 30, 35, 50, 75 and 115, and Employment and Immigration Votes 10 and 25, and Environment Vote 1, and Indian Affairs and Northern Development Votes 30 and 35, and Industry, Science and Technology Vote 25, and Justice Votes 1 and 5, and Labour Vote 5, and National Health and Welfare Vote 15, and Parliament Vote 1, and Solicitor General Vote 10, and Supply and Services Votes 1 and 5 (Schedule F) of the said Estimates, $1,651,563,431.35;
be granted to Her Majesty on account of the fiscal year ending March 31, 1994.
